     {
       "id": "scm_call120_thick_overcast",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS and inside RTRN of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_ref2_120.json). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped extended-column state (TAVEL, TZ, PZ, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, SEMISS, TBOUND) and the GASABS outputs PFRAC and ITR (140 g-points x 103 layers, injected as flattened columns); the gas optics themselves are not transcribed. Expected values: the RTRN fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX and clear-sky TOTUCLFL/TOTDCLFL at every RRTM level, the per-band fluxes at the surface, model top and top of the column, the Planck integrals PLANKBND/PLVL/PLAY, and the heating rates HTR/HTRC (K/day). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: OVERCAST, optically thick. Call 120, 20:00 UTC (13:34 LST), the deepest cirrus deck of the run: RRTM layers 51-57 all have CLDFRAC = 1 with TAUCLOUD 0.054, 0.636, 0.760, 0.467, 0.233, 0.084, 0.024, so the cloud absorptance ABSCLD = 1 - exp(-1.66 TAUCLOUD) reaches 0.72 and EFCLFRAC = ABSCLD (CLDFRAC = 1); this is the regime in which the cloudy branch of the RTRN sweeps (loops 2000/4000, the Pade-weighted total source BBUTOT/BBDLEVD and the combined absorptance ATOT) dominates the transfer. tbound = 285.69 K, glw = 292.8 W/m^2 against a clear-sky 260.9 W/m^2 (a 31.9 W/m^2 surface cloud forcing), olr (model top) = 129.7 W/m^2, TOA upward flux 126.6 W/m^2, and HTR - HTRC reaches 25.0 K/day at layer 52. Tolerances: measured against the real32 dump the component's flux columns agree to Linf 1.3e-4 (F_dn), 2.0e-4 (F_up), 1.0e-4 (F_dn_clr) and 1.8e-4 W/m^2 (F_up_clr) on fluxes up to 371 W/m^2 (3e-7 relative at the spot levels), the band fluxes to 1.2e-5 W/m^2, the Planck integrals to 8.3e-11, and HTR/HTRC to 3.7e-4 / 4.3e-4 K/day on a column maximum of 23.4 K/day (3.3e-6 relative at the three cloud layers spot-checked). Tolerances are set 4-30x above those floors and are the same contract as the other RTRN regimes: fluxes rel 1e-5 spot / Linf abs 1e-3 W/m^2, band fluxes Linf abs 1e-4, Planck Linf abs 1e-9, HTR/HTRC Linf abs 2e-3 K/day and spot checks rel 1e-4 at the three cloudy layers 52, 54 and 55 (the three largest |HTR| of the column).",
