     {
       "id": "scm_call240_fractional_cloud",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS and inside RTRN of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_cloud_240.json, written by the same em_scm_xy run re-executed for 8 h with the cloudy calls added to ESM_DUMP_CALLS; the re-run reproduces the archived call 120 dump bit-for-bit, so it is the same trajectory). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped extended-column state (TAVEL, TZ, PZ, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, SEMISS, TBOUND) and the GASABS outputs PFRAC and ITR (140 g-points x 103 layers, injected as flattened columns); the gas optics themselves are not transcribed. Expected values: the RTRN fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX and clear-sky TOTUCLFL/TOTDCLFL at every RRTM level, the per-band fluxes at the surface, model top and top of the column, the Planck integrals PLANKBND/PLVL/PLAY, and the heating rates HTR/HTRC (K/day). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: FRACTIONAL CLOUD. Call 240, 21:00 UTC (14:34 LST), the decaying cirrus deck: RRTM layer 55 has CLDFRAC = 0.1470 with TAUCLOUD = 0.009966, so ABSCLD = 0.016407 but EFCLFRAC = ABSCLD CLDFRAC = 0.002412 - the only place in the RTRN sweeps where the cloud fraction is not 1 and the two coefficients differ (here by a factor 6.8). MM5ATM forces CLDFRC = 1 wherever TAUCLOUD > 0.01 (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4254), so a layer can only reach RTRN with 0 < CLDFRAC < 1 when its cloud optical depth is at or below 0.01: this layer sits exactly at that ceiling and is therefore the strongest fractional-cloud case the scheme admits. Layers 51-54, 56 and 57 are overcast (TAUCLOUD 0.0728, 0.1423, 0.0709, 0.0403, 0.00475, 0.00296), so the column also exercises fractional and overcast cloudy layers stacked in one sweep. tbound = 285.85 K, glw = 276.6 W/m^2 against a clear-sky 262.8 W/m^2, olr (model top) = 207.4 W/m^2, TOA upward flux 201.7 W/m^2, HTR - HTRC = 2.27 K/day at layer 51 and 0.131 K/day (8.7 % of HTR) in the fractional layer 55. Tolerances: measured against the real32 dump the component's flux columns agree to Linf 1.4e-4 (F_dn), 1.5e-4 (F_up), 1.0e-4 (F_dn_clr) and 2.5e-4 W/m^2 (F_up_clr) on fluxes up to 370 W/m^2 (5e-8 to 5e-7 relative at the spot levels), the band fluxes to 1.1e-5 W/m^2, the Planck integrals to 2.2e-10, and HTR/HTRC to 2.5e-4 / 3.5e-4 K/day. The spot-checked heating rates are small (|HTR| = 1.03, 0.57 and 1.51 K/day at layers 51, 52 and the fractional layer 55), so the same 2.5e-4 K/day floor is 7.3e-5 relative at layer 51; the HTR spot tolerance is therefore rel 2e-4 here instead of the 1e-4 used where |HTR| is large. Everything else is the standard RTRN contract, 4-8x above the measured floors: fluxes rel 1e-5 spot / Linf abs 1e-3 W/m^2, band fluxes Linf abs 1e-4, Planck Linf abs 1e-9, HTR/HTRC Linf abs 2e-3 K/day.",
