       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS and inside RTRN of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_cloud_648.json, written by the same em_scm_xy run re-executed for 8 h with the cloudy calls added to ESM_DUMP_CALLS; the re-run reproduces the archived call 120 dump bit-for-bit, so it is the same trajectory). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped extended-column state (TAVEL, TZ, PZ, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, SEMISS, TBOUND) and the GASABS outputs PFRAC and ITR (140 g-points x 103 layers, injected as flattened columns); the gas optics themselves are not transcribed. Expected values: the RTRN fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX and clear-sky TOTUCLFL/TOTDCLFL at every RRTM level, the per-band fluxes at the surface, model top and top of the column, the Planck integrals PLANKBND/PLVL/PLAY, and the heating rates HTR/HTRC (K/day). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: MULTI-LAYER OVERLAP. Call 648, 01:00 UTC (18:34 LST), thin residual cirrus: three adjacent fractional layers (53: CLDFRAC = 0.0698, TAUCLOUD = 0.00983; 54: 0.0194, 0.00160; 55: 0.0387, 0.00152) sandwiched between overcast layers (52: TAUCLOUD = 0.0237; 56: 0.00138; 57: 0.000387; 59: 6.5e-8), plus a layer with condensate but CLDFRAC = 0 (51, TAUCLOUD = 0.00314, which RTRN treats as clear because ICLDLYR = 0 when CLDFRAC = 0). The sweep therefore passes through clear, fractional and overcast layers in both directions and accumulates the clear-sky radiance from the first cloudy layer downward (ICLDDN, note N31). tbound = 281.17 K, glw = 262.7 W/m^2 against a clear-sky 261.4 W/m^2, olr (model top) = 242.4 W/m^2, TOA upward flux 235.5 W/m^2, HTR - HTRC = 0.099 K/day at layer 51 and 0.015 K/day in the fractional layer 53. Tolerances: measured against the real32 dump the component's flux columns agree to Linf 1.0e-4 (F_dn), 1.6e-4 (F_up), 8.9e-5 (F_dn_clr) and 1.9e-4 W/m^2 (F_up_clr) on fluxes up to 347 W/m^2 (4e-7 relative at the spot levels), the band fluxes to 1.5e-5 W/m^2, the Planck integrals to 1.1e-10, and HTR/HTRC to 2.8e-4 / 2.7e-4 K/day. As at call 240 the spot-checked heating rates are of order 1.3-1.8 K/day, so the flux noise is 5.3e-5 relative at layer 51 and the HTR spot tolerance is rel 2e-4. Everything else is the standard RTRN contract, 4-10x above the measured floors: fluxes rel 1e-5 spot / Linf abs 1e-3 W/m^2, band fluxes Linf abs 1e-4, Planck Linf abs 1e-9, HTR/HTRC Linf abs 2e-3 K/day.",
