     {
       "id": "qss_call268_mixed_phase_storm",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 idealized supercell (em_quarter_ss, Weisman-Klemp sounding, 41 x 41 x 59 mass points, dx = 2 km, dt = 6 s, ztop = 12800 m so p_top = 177.07 hPa and NBUF = 44, i.e. the same 59 + 44 = 103-layer RRTM column as the em_scm_xy regimes) with mp=6 (WSM6), ra_lw=1, ra_sw=1, radt = 5 min, GNU real32 build, dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS and inside RTRN of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump qss_i20_268.json, call 268 = j-row 22 of radiation call 7, column i = 20 selected with the new ESM_DUMP_I). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped extended-column state (TAVEL, TZ, PZ, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, SEMISS, TBOUND) and the GASABS outputs PFRAC and ITR (140 g-points x 103 layers, injected as flattened columns); the gas optics themselves are not transcribed. Expected values: the RTRN fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX and clear-sky TOTUCLFL/TOTDCLFL at every RRTM level, the per-band fluxes at the surface, model top and top of the column, the Planck integrals PLANKBND/PLVL/PLAY, and the heating rates HTR/HTRC (K/day). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: OPAQUE MIXED-PHASE STORM COLUMN -- the saturated limit of the cloudy branch, which the em_scm_xy regimes never reach. Model time 00:30:00 in a mature supercell: 46 of the 59 model layers are overcast (CLDFRAC = 1) and TAUCLOUD runs to 18.74, so ABSCLD = 1 - exp(-1.66 TAUCLOUD) is 1 to within 3e-14 in 25 of them, against a maximum of 0.72 anywhere in the SCM run; exactly one layer (RRTM layer 56, TAUCLOUD = 4.81e-3, below MM5ATM's 0.01 override threshold, N58) keeps a fractional CLDFRAC = 0.010691. tbound = 300.02 K. glw = 451.10 W/m^2 against a clear-sky 405.73 (a 45.4 W/m^2 surface cloud forcing), olr (model top) = 160.52 W/m^2 against a clear-sky 259.46 (the opaque cloud removes 98.9 W/m^2 of outgoing longwave), TOA upward flux 159.30 W/m^2, and HTR - HTRC reaches 41.0 K/day at layer 40, at the ice/liquid cloud top -- 1.6x the largest cloud-radiative heating anywhere in the SCM regimes. Tolerances: measured against the real32 dump the component's flux columns agree to Linf 1.8e-4 (F_dn), 1.5e-4 (F_up), 2.2e-4 (F_dn_clr) and 2.0e-4 W/m^2 (F_up_clr) on fluxes up to 458 W/m^2 (<= 4.0e-7 relative at the spot levels), the band fluxes to 1.2e-5 W/m^2, the Planck integrals to 2.0e-10, and HTR/HTRC to 2.0e-4 / 2.6e-4 K/day on a column maximum of 43.5 K/day (<= 2.1e-6 relative at the three cloud-top layers spot-checked). Tolerances are set 5-50x above those floors and are the same contract as the other RTRN regimes: fluxes rel 1e-5 spot / Linf abs 1e-3 W/m^2, band fluxes Linf abs 1e-4, Planck Linf abs 1e-9, HTR/HTRC Linf abs 2e-3 K/day and spot checks rel 1e-4 at layers 39, 40 and 41, the three largest |HTR| of the column.",
